{marker acknowledgments}{...}
{title:Acknowledgments}

{pstd}
{cmd:cjoinby} reimplements {cmd:joinby}, an official Stata command. Its
syntax, options, {cmd:_merge} variable, value label, and messages follow
{cmd:joinby}.

{pstd}
{cmd:cjoinby} is pinned to this version of {cmd:joinby}:

{p2colset 9 27 29 2}{...}
{p2col:Command}{cmd:joinby} (official Stata){p_end}
{p2col:Authors}StataCorp LLC{p_end}
{p2col:Version}{cmd:joinby.ado} 2.1.0{p_end}
{p2col:Date}December 22, 2022{p_end}
{p2col:Header line}{cmd:*! version 2.1.0  22dec2022}{p_end}
{p2col:Shipped with}StataNow 19.5 (revision 14 Oct 2026){p_end}
{p2colreset}{...}

{pstd}
{cmd:cjoinby} follows {cmd:joinby} as it behaves in this Stata release.
{cmd:which joinby} shows the version of {cmd:joinby.ado} in your Stata.
{help ctools##acknowledgments:help ctools} lists the pinned versions of all
ctools commands.

{pstd}
Please report bugs and questions about {cmd:cjoinby} at
{browse "https://github.com/mdroste/stata-ctools/issues":github.com/mdroste/stata-ctools/issues}.
StataCorp does not support {cmd:cjoinby}. Undocumented differences between
{cmd:cjoinby} and {cmd:joinby} are bugs in {cmd:cjoinby}.
{* ctools-attribution:end}{...}


